/* Simple (1:1) Unicode case mapping, as ranges of code points that share
 * one offset. GENERATED by scripts/case-contract/probe.dawn -- do not edit;
 * scripts/case-contract/run.sh walks it against the same oracle, code
 * point by code point, and names what disagreed.
 *
 * The JVM backend calls Character.toUpperCase/toLowerCase, which *is* this
 * mapping, so this table is how the C runtime answers the same function.
 * Full mapping (the one where a sharp s uppercases to two letters) is
 * locale- and context-sensitive and belongs in a library, not here.
 *
 * The oracle is a JDK, and a JDK carries one Unicode release, so which one
 * answered is part of the data. The contract compares this against the JDK
 * it runs on and refuses to judge across a difference. */
